7,Kagoro — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kagoro,"The Kagoro, also known as Gworok, Aegworok, or Agworok, are an indigenous ethnic group of approximately 37,000 people primarily residing in the Kagoro chiefdom of southern Kaduna State, Nigeria. [1] They inhabit the town of Kagoro in the Kaura Local Government Area and speak a dialect subgroup of Tyap, a Niger-Congo language of the Plateau branch. [1] Predominantly Neo-Pentecostal Christians ...",Kagoro,Niger-Congo
